let __v_110 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$dict\":[[\"the wire\",\"*The Wire* is worth it, and the slow start is the point - give it four or five episodes. Five series, a whole city in it, and it does not go soft at the end.\"],[\"breaking bad\",\"Yes. Short episodes, five series, and it gets darker every year without losing the plot; Bryan Cranston is the reason it works.\"],[\"better call saul\",\"Slower than *Breaking Bad* on purpose, and worth the patience if you liked that one: it is a long, careful fall and it sticks the ending.\"],[\"the sopranos\",\"Yes - the drama that started the run of great telly. Six series, and a last scene people are still arguing about.\"],[\"succession\",\"Yes: four series of a family at each other's throats, and much funnier than it sounds. If you liked *The Thick of It*, start tonight.\"],[\"fleabag\",\"An easy yes, and it takes about one evening: two series of six short episodes, funny first and then quietly devastating.\"],[\"happy valley\",\"Three series and Sarah Lancashire is extraordinary in it; the third is the best of them.\"],[\"line of duty\",\"Six series of interviews and bent coppers - start at the first one, because the story builds rather than resets.\"],[\"peaky blinders\",\"Six series, very stylish, and a bit of a slog in the middle; Cillian Murphy is the reason to watch it.\"],[\"chernobyl\",\"Five episodes and the best short drama about a disaster ever made. Worth one evening even if you think you know the story.\"],[\"the bear\",\"Yes, and the episodes are about half an hour: loud, stressful, and really about a family, with a sandwich shop round it.\"],[\"ted lasso\",\"Warm and funny, and the first series is the best of the three - if you want something kind on a wet evening, this is it.\"],[\"schitts creek\",\"Worth it, but start knowing the first series is the weakest: it finds its feet in the second and the last one is a joy.\"],[\"derry girls\",\"Three short series and properly funny; the last one has the Good Friday Agreement underneath it and still makes you laugh.\"],[\"game of thrones\",\"Worth it, with a warning: most people hate the last series. The first six are as good as television gets.\"],[\"the crown\",\"Six series, each with a new cast, and the first two with Claire Foy are the best; watch those and decide whether to go on.\"],[\"stranger things\",\"The first series is the one - 80s, kids on bikes, a monster. It gets bigger and sillier after that, so treat the later ones as a bonus.\"],[\"sherlock\",\"Four short series of 90-minute episodes, and the first two are the good ones; start with 'A Study in Pink'.\"],[\"black mirror\",\"It is an anthology, so pick the standouts first - 'San Junipero' and 'USS Callister' - and skip around rather than in order.\"],[\"killing eve\",\"The first series is brilliant; it gets weaker after that, but Jodie Comer is worth staying for.\"],[\"mad men\",\"Seven series in a 1960s ad agency: slow, stylish and really about people lying to themselves. Give it three episodes.\"],[\"downton abbey\",\"Six series of a country house upstairs and down; gentle, easy and very watchable if you want something undemanding.\"],[\"only murders in the building\",\"Yes - a funny whodunnit with two older men and a young woman, three series of short episodes.\"],[\"the traitors\",\"Genuinely gripping for a reality show; the UK version is the one to start with and the round tables are the best part.\"],[\"doctor who\",\"Start with the 2005 revival rather than the old ones: each episode stands alone, and the first series with Christopher Eccleston is a good way in.\"],[\"pride and prejudice\",\"Worth reading, and funnier than school makes it sound - give it three chapters and you will know whether you get on with it.\"],[\"1984\",\"Yes, and it is shorter and bleaker than most people expect; the middle is a long essay about power and the story around it is what stays.\"],[\"to kill a mockingbird\",\"Worth it: a child's-eye view of a court case, and the first half is slow on purpose - it is setting up what you will care about.\"],[\"dune\",\"Worth it either way: the film tells the story cleanly and you do not need the book first. The book is denser and better on the politics, and both start slowly.\"],[\"the office\",\"Yes, and start with the UK one - twelve episodes and then it is over, so it costs you an evening to find out. The US one is gentler and much longer.\"],[\"oppenheimer\",\"Worth it in a cinema if you can, because the sound is half of it; three hours of men in rooms that somehow never drags.\"],[\"the godfather\",\"Yes, and it holds up: the first two are the ones. Part three is the one people argue about, so leave it until you care.\"],[\"lord of the rings\",\"The fellowship one is the place to start, and the extended cut is worth it once you know you like it - three hours a film, so give it a free evening.\"],[\"harry potter\",\"Worth it, and the books hold up better than the films for a reader past ten; the third book is where it gets properly good.\"],[\"gone girl\",\"Worth it: a thriller that turns halfway and takes you with it. The film is faithful, so pick either one and skip the other.\"],[\"my neighbour totoro\",\"Worth it at any age: gentle, almost nothing goes wrong, and it is the film for a rainy afternoon or after a bad week. 86 minutes, and no baddie to speak of.\"],[\"spirited away\",\"Yes - the best way into Studio Ghibli and the one that wins over people who say they do not like animation. Subtitled if you can; the English voices are good too.\"],[\"parasite\",\"Yes, and go in knowing nothing: it turns about halfway and the less you know the better. Subtitles, two hours, and it never feels long.\"],[\"paddington 2\",\"The rare sequel better than the first: warm, funny, and Hugh Grant having the time of his life. The safest film there is for a mixed-age evening.\"],[\"everything everywhere all at once\",\"Worth it if you have the energy for it: two hours twenty of noise, jokes and feeling, and the last twenty minutes earn all of it. Have tissues.\"],[\"squid game\",\"Yes - the first series is the one to start with: one game an episode, and the tension is in the rules rather than the blood. The later series are slower, so only go on if you liked the first.\"],[\"the last of us\",\"Worth it even if you never played the game: nine episodes, and the third one is a whole love story with almost nobody else in it. Bleak, so not a background watch.\"],[\"shogun\",\"Yes - a stranger in a strange court, and it is about power and translation more than battles. Partly subtitled, and better for it.\"],[\"slow horses\",\"Yes: Gary Oldman as a filthy, brilliant spymaster, six short series, and it gets funnier as it gets darker. Start at the first.\"],[\"severance\",\"Worth it: office workers whose memories are split between work and home, and the slowest drip of information you will be glad of. Short episodes, and pay attention.\"],[\"the boys\",\"Yes if you like your superheroes filthy and angry - it is a satire with a lot of gore. If you want charm, this is not it.\"],[\"money heist\",\"Worth it for the first two parts, which are one long heist with a hostage negotiator; the later parts stretch a good idea a long way. Try the original audio rather than the dub.\"],[\"bridgerton\",\"Yes if you want gorgeous, silly, warm romance: each series is one couple and a lot of string-quartet pop. It is not trying to be serious.\"],[\"the witcher\",\"The first series is confusing on purpose and settles by the second; watch it for the monster-of-the-week episodes and Henry Cavill's growl.\"],[\"gilmore girls\",\"Worth it: seven series of very fast talking, a small town, and a mother and daughter who are friends. Comfort television rather than plot.\"],[\"sex education\",\"Yes - four series, funny and kind, about a teenager running an advice clinic at school, with Gillian Anderson as his mother.\"],[\"normal people\",\"Worth it: two people circling each other over twelve short episodes, and the most honest silences on television. Bleak in a quiet way.\"],[\"bluey\",\"Yes, and not only for the children: seven-minute episodes about a family of dogs that are funnier and sadder than they need to be, and a parent gets more out of it than the child.\"],[\"avatar the last airbender\",\"Worth it: three series of a cartoon that is really a war story with a twelve-year-old in the middle, and it earns its ending. Start at episode one, not the film.\"],[\"the matrix\",\"Yes, and it holds up: the first film is the one, and the effects still work because they serve the story. The sequels are for people who want more of the world.\"],[\"inception\",\"Worth it: a heist inside dreams, and it explains its own rules as it goes. Watch it without your phone and the ending lands.\"],[\"interstellar\",\"Yes, on the biggest screen you can: a father-and-daughter story with a black hole in the middle, and the sound is half of it. The middle act is slow.\"],[\"everything everywhere all at once\",\"Yes, and give it twenty minutes: it is silly and fast and then it is about a mother and a daughter and you are crying. The middle is a lot of noise.\"],[\"barbie\",\"Worth it: funny and strange and about more than the doll, and Ryan Gosling steals it. Two hours, and it knows exactly what it is doing.\"],[\"wonka\",\"Worth it for a family evening: warm, colourful, songs you half know, and Chalamet is charming. Nobody needed it, but it is a good time.\"],[\"the holdovers\",\"Yes - a grumpy teacher, a stranded student and a cook at a boarding school over Christmas. Small, funny, and it earns its ending.\"],[\"past lives\",\"Worth it: two childhood friends in different countries and twenty years of what-ifs. Quiet, short, and it does not go where you expect.\"],[\"where the crawdads sing\",\"Worth it if you want a slow, sad mystery about a girl raising herself in a marsh. The book is better and the film is faithful to it.\"],[\"the midnight library\",\"Worth it: a woman between life and death tries the lives she did not live. Gentle, quick, and the ending is the argument.\"],[\"lessons in chemistry\",\"Yes - a chemist in the 1960s turns a cooking show into a lecture, and it is funny and angry at once. A dog narrates a chapter.\"],[\"the seven husbands of evelyn hugo\",\"Worth it: an old film star tells her life story to a reporter, and it is a soap opera in the best sense.\"],[\"tomorrow and tomorrow and tomorrow\",\"Yes - two friends making video games over thirty years, and it is really about work, and love, and the friend you do not marry.\"],[\"a little life\",\"Worth it, but be warned: it is long, it is about damage, and it is relentless. Read it when you have a fortnight and somebody to talk to about it.\"],[\"klara and the sun\",\"Worth it: an artificial friend watches a family and misunderstands beautifully. Quiet, and the ending stays with you.\"],[\"the song of achilles\",\"Yes - the Iliad told by Patroclus, and it is a love story first and a war epic second. Have the tissues ready.\"],[\"circe\",\"Worth it: the witch of the Odyssey tells her own story, and it is about power and exile. Slow to start, then it grips.\"],[\"piranesi\",\"Worth it, and go in knowing nothing: a man lives in an infinite house of statues. Short, strange, and the reveal is the reward.\"],[\"project hail mary\",\"Yes - a man wakes alone on a spaceship and has to science his way out, with one very funny alien. Best read cold.\"],[\"the martian\",\"Worth it: one man, one planet, and a lot of problem-solving, and the most cheerful survival story there is.\"],[\"sapiens\",\"Worth it as an argument rather than a history: bracing and readable, and confidently wrong in places, so read it with a pinch of salt.\"]]}")?;
