let __v_718 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$dict\":[[\"guitar\",\"Clip a tuner on the headstock and take the string order low to high: E, A, D, G, B, E - the sixth string is the thick one, and the top E is the thin one. Turn the peg slowly and always come up to the note from below, because slackening down to it leaves the string ready to slip. Ten seconds a string, and tune every time you pick it up; guitars move with the room.\"],[\"bass\",\"A clip-on tuner and the string order low to high: E, A, D, G. Turn the peg slowly and come up to each note from below rather than down onto it. A bass needs tuning less often than a guitar but goes out if the room changes temperature.\"],[\"ukulele\",\"Clip-on tuner, and the four strings low to high are G, C, E, A - the top G is the one people get wrong, because on a ukulele it is the higher G, not the lowest note. Turn the peg in small movements and check the string again after you play a chord: nylon strings settle slowly and need a week of retuning when they are new.\"],[\"violin\",\"A clip-on tuner and the order G, D, A, E from the lowest string up - and the pegs are for the big jumps while the fine tuners at the tailpiece do the last bit. Turn the peg with a little inward pressure so it grips, or it will slip as soon as you let go.\"],[\"piano\",\"An upright or grand is a job for a tuner, not for you: an annual visit, and twice a year if it is in a room that gets hot in summer. A digital piano needs nothing. If one note has gone badly wrong on an acoustic, stop playing it and get the tuner in, because it is usually a string or a hammer rather than the tuning.\"]]}")?;
