let __v_1148 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$dict\":[[\"sad\",\"For a good cry: *Manchester by the Sea* is quiet and devastating, *Atonement* lands its ending like a brick, and *Up* does it in the first ten minutes. Have tissues ready.\"],[\"funny\",\"For laughs: *What We Do in the Shadows* (a daft vampire mockumentary), *The Nice Guys* (funny and twisty) or *Paddington 2*, which makes almost everyone laugh.\"],[\"think\",\"*Arrival* (would you want to know the future?), *12 Angry Men* (one room, all talk, gripping) or *Ex Machina* (quiet, unsettling science fiction). All three stay with you afterwards.\"],[\"uplifting\",\"*Hunt for the Wilderpeople* (funny and warm), *The Shawshank Redemption* (hope you have to earn) or *Sing Street* (music, first love and a big grin at the end).\"],[\"gripping\",\"*Prisoners* is tense from the first scene, *Gone Girl* keeps you guessing to the end, and *Sicario* turns the screw for two hours straight.\"],[\"short\",\"*Before Sunset* runs 80 minutes, *Locke* is 85 with one man in a car, and *Toy Story* is 81. All three are short and none of them asks much of a tired evening.\"],[\"true\",\"*Zodiac* (the investigation, not the killings), *Catch Me If You Can* (light and a lot of fun) or *127 Hours* if you want to be on the edge of your seat.\"],[\"twist\",\"*The Sixth Sense*, *The Prestige* and *Gone Girl* all turn on a twist you will not see coming. Start with *The Prestige*.\"],[\"romance\",\"*Before Sunrise* (two people talking all night), *When Harry Met Sally* (the funny one) or *Pride & Prejudice* (2005) for the longing and the costumes.\"],[\"light\",\"*Paddington 2*, *Chef* or *The Detectorists* (a series): warm, low-stakes and easy to watch, and nothing bad happens in any of them.\"]]}")?;
frame.store("FILM_MOODS", __v_1148.clone())?;
let __v_1149 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$dict\":[[\"sad\",\"*A Little Life* is the one people sob through, *Never Let Me Go* hurts quietly, and *The Kite Runner* if you want it to hit hard.\"],[\"scary\",\"*The Haunting of Hill House* is creepy rather than gory, *Bird Box* is fast and tense, and *The Shining* if you want the classic.\"],[\"think\",\"*Klara and the Sun* (what makes someone human), *The Remains of the Day* (a whole life looked back on) or *Sapiens* if you would rather have ideas than a story.\"],[\"uplifting\",\"*The Midnight Library* (gentle and hopeful), *Lessons in Chemistry* (funny and big-hearted) or *The Hundred-Year-Old Man Who Climbed Out of the Window and Disappeared* (daft and warm).\"],[\"gripping\",\"*Gone Girl* (twisty from page one), *The Martian* (problem-solving and very hard to put down) or any *Jack Reacher* book by Lee Child.\"],[\"short\",\"*Of Mice and Men* is about 100 pages, *The Old Man and the Sea* is short and perfect, and *Small Things Like These* is under 120 pages.\"],[\"true\",\"*Educated* by Tara Westover, *Into the Wild* by Jon Krakauer or *The Diary of a Young Girl* by Anne Frank: all real, all hard to stop reading.\"],[\"twist\",\"*The Silent Patient* and *Gone Girl* both turn on a twist; *The Seven Husbands of Evelyn Hugo* if you want the reveal to make you cry as well.\"],[\"romance\",\"*The Flatshare* (funny and warm), *Beach Read* (a bit sharper) or *Pride and Prejudice* if you want the classic.\"],[\"light\",\"*The Thursday Murder Club* (funny and gentle), *The Midnight Library* or *The No. 1 Ladies' Detective Agency*: easy to pick up and nothing grim.\"]]}")?;
frame.store("BOOK_MOODS", __v_1149.clone())?;
let __v_1150 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$dict\":[[\"sad\",\"*This Is Us* is built to make you cry weekly, *Normal People* hurts quietly, and *After Life* mixes the sad with real jokes.\"],[\"funny\",\"*Schitt's Creek* starts daft and gets warmer, *Derry Girls* is sharp and short, and *The Detectorists* is gentle comedy.\"],[\"think\",\"*Severance* (what work does to a person), *Chernobyl* (how a system fails) or *The Wire* if you want a whole city to think about.\"],[\"uplifting\",\"*Ted Lasso* is kind and funny, *The Repair Shop* is people mending things that matter to them, and *Call the Midwife* if you want warmth and a cry.\"],[\"gripping\",\"*Happy Valley* is tense from the first scene, *The Night Of* does not let go, and *Bodyguard* starts at a sprint and stays there.\"],[\"short\",\"Episodes beat films when the evening is short: *The Bear* is 25 minutes an episode, *Derry Girls* is 22, and *Inside No. 9* is half an hour with a twist.\"],[\"true\",\"*The Long Shadow*, *Des* or *Mr Bates vs The Post Office*: true stories told straight, all of them hard to stop watching.\"],[\"twist\",\"*Line of Duty* for the reveal at the end of every series, *Severance* for the strangest one, and *Broadchurch* if you like a whole town hiding something.\"],[\"romance\",\"*Normal People* for the intense one, *Starstruck* for the funny one, and *Bridgerton* if you want the frocks and the gossip.\"],[\"scary\",\"*The Haunting of Hill House* for dread, *Midnight Mass* if you want one with ideas in it, and *Inside No. 9* for half-hour creepers.\"],[\"light\",\"*The Detectorists* is the gentlest thing on telly, *Mortimer & Whitehouse: Gone Fishing* is two friends chatting, and *The Great British Bake Off* needs no attention at all.\"]]}")?;
frame.store("TV_MOODS", __v_1150.clone())?;
let __v_1151 = Value::from("For funny: *No Such Thing as a Fish* (four people, one bizarre fact each, about half an hour), *The Adam Buxton Podcast* for long chats that wander, or *Off Menu* where guests order their dream meal. All easy to dip in and out of.");
frame.store("PODCAST_FUNNY", __v_1151.clone())?;
let __v_1152 = Value::from("*Serial* series one is where to start: one murder, a year of reporting, and the reason everyone else started making them. Then *Casefile* (calm, one case an episode), *Criminal* (short, strange cases, less grim) or *The Teacher's Pet* if you want one long story done properly.");
frame.store("PODCAST_CRIME", __v_1152.clone())?;
