let __v_2701 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$dict\":[[\"cooking\",\"For cooking: *MasterChef: The Professionals* is the one about the cooking itself, *The Great British Bake Off* for baking and *Saturday Kitchen* for a lazy morning, all of them long-running and easy to start anywhere.\"],[\"baking\",\"*The Great British Bake Off* is the gentle one everybody watches, *Bake Off: The Professionals* if you want skill, and *Paul Hollywood* travel shows if it is the bread you care about.\"],[\"gardening\",\"*Gardeners' World* is the one that tells you what to do this week, *Beechgrove* for a colder climate and *Love Your Garden* for the before-and-after. Start with Gardeners' World and its monthly jobs.\"],[\"nature\",\"*Planet Earth II* is the best of them, *Blue Planet II* for the sea and *Springwatch* for British wildlife in real time. The first two look astonishing on any television.\"],[\"history\",\"*The World at War* is the one people still cite, *Time Team* for digging and Lucy Worsley's series for the social side. All three are old and none of them feel dated.\"],[\"science\",\"Brian Cox's *The Planets* is the easy way into space, *Forces of Nature* for how the world works, and *Chemistry: A Volatile History* if you would rather have the story of the ideas.\"],[\"sport\",\"*The Last Dance* is the one that grips people who do not follow basketball, *Sunderland 'Til I Die* for football and *Welcome to Wrexham* if you want to enjoy one. All three are about the people, not the scores.\"],[\"true crime\",\"*The Jinx* is the one with the ending nobody saw coming, *The Staircase* for the long haul, and *Des* for a British one with David Tennant. All three are about the case rather than the killings.\"],[\"quiz\",\"*Only Connect* is the cleverest thing on television, *Would I Lie to You?* is the funniest panel show and *University Challenge* the most tense. Start with Would I Lie to You? for a group.\"],[\"property\",\"*Grand Designs* for the build, *Location, Location, Location* for the search and *The Great Interior Design Challenge* if you want the rooms. Grand Designs is the one with the arguments.\"],[\"travel\",\"*Travel Man* for a city in 48 hours, *Race Across the World* for the long way round and any of Michael Palin's journeys for the old-fashioned version. Travel Man is the short one.\"],[\"repair\",\"*The Repair Shop* is the warm one about people mending things that matter to them, *Long Lost Family* for the other kind of mending, and *Salvage Hunters* if you like the hunt.\"],[\"documentary\",\"*Free Solo* for one man on a cliff, *The Jinx* for a case that turns, and *Planet Earth II* for the pictures. None of the three needs any background to enjoy.\"]]}")?;
