let __v_3212 = Value::from("*Saga* by Brian K. Vaughan is the usual first pick for an adult: a space story with a family at its centre and art that carries the plot. *Watchmen* if you want the one that changed what comics could do, *Persepolis* by Marjane Satrapi for a memoir told this way, and *Heartstopper* by Alice Oseman for a warm school romance. For manga, *Death Note* or *One Piece* is where most people start. Begin with a complete story rather than a forty-year superhero run, and a library will lend all of these.");
frame.store("_COMIC_FOR_A_GROWN_UP", __v_3212.clone())?;
let __v_3213 = Value::from("*Death Note* (a notebook that kills, and the duel that follows) is the usual first manga: twelve volumes, a clean ending, and nothing to know beforehand. *One Piece* if they want a long one to live in, or *Fullmetal Alchemist* if they would rather have something they can finish. Read right to left, back to front - the pages are printed the Japanese way.");
frame.store("_COMIC_MANGA", __v_3213.clone())?;
let __v_3214 = Value::from("*Daredevil: Born Again* by Frank Miller is the one to start with: short, brutal and complete in itself. *Hawkeye* by Matt Fraction if you want funny, *Ms Marvel* by G. Willow Wilson if you want a teenager finding her feet. Skip the crossover events - they assume forty years of reading behind them.");
frame.store("_COMIC_MARVEL", __v_3214.clone())?;
let __v_3215 = Value::from("*Batman: Year One* by Frank Miller is the cleanest way in: one short story, no homework. *All-Star Superman* by Grant Morrison if you want the character at his best, *Swamp Thing* by Alan Moore if you want something strange and grown-up. *Watchmen* is the other DC one worth the time.");
frame.store("_COMIC_DC", __v_3215.clone())?;
let __v_3216 = Value::from("*Bone* by Jeff Smith is the easiest place to start: one long story, funny, and it looks like a children's book until you are deep in it. *Persepolis* by Marjane Satrapi if you want something true, *Saga* if you want a space story. A library will have all three, and one complete story is a better first comic than a run of forty issues.");
frame.store("_COMIC_BEGINNER", __v_3216.clone())?;
let __v_3217 = Value::from("A graphic novel is one whole story told in comic panels and published as a single book rather than a monthly issue - *Persepolis* and *Watchmen* are the classic examples. Manga is Japanese comics, usually printed right to left, and *Death Note* is an easy first one.");
frame.store("_COMIC_MEANING", __v_3217.clone())?;
