let __v_6555 = Value::from("Start with the rhythm, not the notes: clap a line of the music while a metronome clicks, because the note names are the easy half. Then learn the five lines of the treble staff with a mnemonic you make up, ten minutes a day, and read one new short piece slowly each day rather than the same one until it is perfect - reading is the skill of playing what you have not seen before.");
frame.store("_PRACTICE_READ_MUSIC", __v_6555.clone())?;
let __v_6556 = Value::from("Fifteen to twenty minutes a day beats two hours on Sunday, and start with the hardest four bars rather than the beginning: play them slowly enough to get them right, four times in a row, then put them back in the piece. Use a metronome at a speed you can play cleanly and nudge it up two beats a minute, because sloppy and fast teaches sloppy. Scales and one technical exercise first warm the hands up, and finish on something you enjoy so you want to come back tomorrow.");
