let __v_6805 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"science\",{\"$tuple\":[\"science\",\"scientific\",\"physics\",\"chemistry\",\"biology\",\"space\",\"astronomy\",\"the universe\",\"nature\",\"wildlife\",\"animals\",\"climate\",\"climate change\",\"environment\",\"ecology\",\"engineering\",\"maths\",\"mathematics\"]},\"For science with jokes: *The Infinite Monkey Cage*, a physicist and a comedian on one question in 45 minutes. *Science Vs* takes one claim an episode and weighs the evidence, and *Ologies* is a long friendly interview with a scientist each time. For space, *13 Minutes to the Moon* is the best thing made about Apollo.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"food\",{\"$tuple\":[\"food\",\"foods\",\"cooking\",\"cook\",\"chef\",\"chefs\",\"baking\",\"bake\",\"recipes\",\"recipe\",\"kitchen\",\"restaurants\",\"eating\"]},\"*Home Cooking* (Samin Nosrat and Hrishikesh Hirway) answers listeners' kitchen questions and is the friendliest place to start. *The Sporkful* is about how and why people eat what they eat, and *Gastropod* takes one food an episode and does its history and science.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"health\",{\"$tuple\":[\"health\",\"healthy\",\"medicine\",\"medical\",\"doctor\",\"sleep\",\"insomnia\",\"fitness\",\"exercise\",\"running\",\"nutrition\",\"diet\",\"weight\",\"mental health\",\"anxiety\",\"stress\",\"wellbeing\"]},\"For health with the evidence shown: *Zoe Science & Nutrition*, one food or habit an episode with a scientist and a doctor. For sleep, *Nothing Much Happens* reads quiet stories slowly and *Sleep With Me* rambles on purpose, both made to send you off rather than to be listened to.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"sport\",{\"$tuple\":[\"sport\",\"sports\",\"football\",\"cricket\",\"rugby\",\"tennis\",\"f1\",\"formula 1\",\"boxing\",\"golf\",\"athletics\",\"cycling\",\"match\",\"matches\"]},\"For football, *Football Weekly* from the Guardian is twice a week, quick and funny, and *The Rest Is Football* is Lineker, Richards and Shearer talking. For cricket, *Tailenders* is the one people who do not like cricket listen to.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"technology\",{\"$tuple\":[\"tech\",\"technology\",\"technologies\",\"gadgets\",\"computer\",\"computers\",\"phone\",\"phones\",\"ai\",\"artificial intelligence\",\"internet\",\"software\",\"programming\",\"coding\",\"cyber\",\"hacking\"]},\"*Hard Fork* (Kevin Roose and Casey Newton) is the weekly one on what the tech companies just did, and it is funny. *Darknet Diaries* is true stories of hacks and the people who did them, and *The Vergecast* is the long argument about gadgets.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"news\",{\"$tuple\":[\"news\",\"politics\",\"political\",\"current affairs\",\"world\",\"election\",\"elections\",\"government\"]},\"*The Daily* takes one story a day and reports it properly in 20 minutes, *Today in Focus* does the same from a British side, and *The Briefing Room* explains one running story with the people who know it. For business, *The Bottom Line* puts three chief executives in a room and asks them the same question.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"people\",{\"$tuple\":[\"psychology\",\"psychologist\",\"human behaviour\",\"human behavior\",\"behaviour\",\"behavior\",\"relationships\",\"relationship\",\"feelings\",\"emotions\",\"people\",\"mindfulness\",\"meditation\",\"habits\"]},\"*Hidden Brain* is the one to start with: one piece of psychology an episode, told as a story. *The Happiness Lab* is the research on what actually makes people happier, and *Where Should We Begin?* is Esther Perel with one real couple in a single session.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"parenting\",{\"$tuple\":[\"parenting\",\"parent\",\"parents\",\"babies\",\"baby\",\"newborn\",\"toddler\",\"kids\",\"children\",\"family\",\"families\",\"motherhood\",\"fatherhood\"]},\"*Parenting Hell* (Rob Beckett and Josh Widdicombe) is two fathers being honest about how badly it is going, which is the most reassuring thing on the subject. *Happy Mum Happy Baby* is the calmer interview version, one parent an episode.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"music\",{\"$tuple\":[\"music\",\"songs\",\"song\",\"albums\",\"album\",\"bands\",\"band\",\"guitar\",\"singing\"]},\"*Song Exploder* takes one song and has the person who made it pull it apart, track by track, in 20 minutes. *Desert Island Discs* is the long interview with the music choices in it, and *All Songs Considered* is the weekly new-music one.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"business\",{\"$tuple\":[\"business\",\"businesses\",\"company\",\"companies\",\"startup\",\"startups\",\"start a business\",\"starting a business\",\"entrepreneur\",\"entrepreneurs\",\"selling\",\"sales\",\"marketing\",\"the economy\",\"economy\",\"economics\",\"finance\",\"financial\"]},\"*How I Built This* has the founder of one company telling how it actually started, in an hour, and it is the most useful one if you are thinking of starting something. *The Bottom Line* puts three bosses in a room and asks them the same question, and *StartUp* follows one company from the first day, mistakes included.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"gardening\",{\"$tuple\":[\"garden\",\"gardening\",\"gardens\",\"allotment\",\"allotments\",\"vegetables\",\"plants\",\"lawn\",\"grow your own\"]},\"*Gardeners' Question Time* is the one to start with: three experts answering listeners' questions, so you get the answer to the thing you were wondering about. *Talking Gardens* is the interview version and *The RHS Podcast* the seasonal jobs.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"film\",{\"$tuple\":[\"film\",\"films\",\"movie\",\"movies\",\"cinema\",\"tv\",\"television\",\"series\",\"telly\"]},\"*The Rewatchables* is one film an episode and why it still works, which is the best listen for someone who likes films. *Kermode & Mayo's Take* reviews what is out now, and *You Must Remember This* tells the old Hollywood stories properly.\"]}]}")?;
